  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Buff Bar",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Buff Bar\"**\n\nThe app is a set of game windows floating over a sky. Each section is a framed window: a dark outer rim, a wooden (by day) or navy (by night) frame with a bright inner bevel, a glossy title bar, and a warm body. The one signature device is the buff slot plus gauge: a target's icon sits in a beveled slot, and when its full length is known, a pill gauge drains under it and turns red near the end. Titles, status words and every number use one chunky rounded face with outlined, drop-stamped numerals, the way game UIs print damage and timers.\n\nThe world arrives only through type, color, density and that one device; the controls themselves stay standard (native buttons, checkboxes, range sliders, `<details>`, `<dialog>`). The screen is an Operate surface: people set things up, confirm \"감시 중\" in the status window, then hide the tab and listen. Nothing animates for decoration; the only motion is state (gem beat, card flash, gauge drain, chevron turn), and all of it honors reduced motion.\n\nLight and dark are two full worlds, not an inverted palette: light is the older-game look (sky, wood, ember title bars, brown ink), dark is the newer-game look (deep navy, navy frames with a pale blue inner line, gold title lettering). Both follow `prefers-color-scheme`; there is no manual toggle. This is an original design that evokes the genre. It uses no real game assets, logos, characters, UI sprites, or the official game typeface.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Framed game windows: rim, frame with inner bevel, title bar, body.",
      "Buff slot plus draining gauge as the single signature device.",
      "Jua Tabular for titles, states, numerals and chips; system Korean sans for body.",
      "Outlined, drop-stamped numerals and title lettering.",
      "Two complete tonal worlds (sky/wood, navy/gold) chosen by the OS.",
      "Standard controls, chunky inner-bevel buttons."
    ],
