        "body": "warn-text, alert-bg, muted and accent stay plain hex custom properties (`--warn-text`, `--alert-bg`, `--muted`, `--accent`); a regression test reads them as strings starting with `#`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Worlds Rule",
        "body": "Every color token has a light and a dark value in the same `:root`/`@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` pair. Never add a color that exists in one tone only.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Color Rule",
        "body": "Green, red and blue mean ok, alert and test. Do not use them for decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Weight Rule",
        "body": "Jua is set at 400 everywhere; emphasis comes from size, color and outline, never a faux bold.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Digits Rule",
        "body": "Every changing number is set in Jua Tabular so its width does not jitter as it counts down.",
        "section": "typography"
